Hours: Wednesday - Sunday, 8:00 - 4:30



From: Robert Samuel White <rsw@rswfire.com>
Sent: Friday, February 7, 2025 3:27 PM
To: ALLEGRA Franki * OPRD <Franki.ALLEGRA@oprd.oregon.gov>
Subject: Re: September

Oh, man. Now Paiute has gotten back to me.

I do not know what to do.

I don't think I'm allowed to go home.

If I stay, I may never see my mom again.

She tells me to stay. I need to think about it.

Is the position in September available to me if I change my mind?

I understand if it's not. I really need to think about this.

I feel so torn.

I'm sorry I'm even troubling you with this.

I get that you have very clear boundaries.

I don't know how to separate my volunteer work from my personal life - they=
 are the same things to me.



________________________________
From: Robert Samuel White <rsw@rswfire.com<mailto:rsw@rswfire.com>>
Sent: Friday, February 7, 2025 1:19:13 PM
To: ALLEGRA Franki * OPRD <Franki.ALLEGRA@oprd.oregon.gov<mailto:Franki.ALL=
EGRA@oprd.oregon.gov>>
Subject: Re: September

Thanks Franki! I'll see you in April!

________________________________
From: ALLEGRA Franki * OPRD <Franki.ALLEGRA@oprd.oregon.gov<mailto:Franki.A=
LLEGRA@oprd.oregon.gov>>
Sent: Friday, February 7, 2025 12:56:09 PM
To: Robert Samuel White <rsw@rswfire.com<mailto:rsw@rswfire.com>>
Subject: Re: September

Hi Sam, that's alright! Canceling well in advance doesn't cause any problem=
s. Everyone understands that things come up!
________________________________
From: Robert Samuel White <rsw@rswfire.com<mailto:rsw@rswfire.com>>
Sent: Thursday, February 6, 2025 11:59:24 PM
To: ALLEGRA Franki * OPRD <franki.allegra@oprd.oregon.gov<mailto:franki.all=
egra@oprd.oregon.gov>>
Subject: Re: September

If this would hurt me in any way, I will stay. I just want to be perfectly =
clear about that. I bring it up now because I'm planning my movements and t=
here are seven months before this assignment, so I trust I wouldn't inconve=
nience you - the timing, like everything, is a variable in my contemplation=
s. I would stay, joyfully, not as a concession, as total acceptance of alig=
nment. I make this plea because I don't have assignments for July and Augus=
t but that time is too short for me to go to Kentucky and back, and I could=
n't go after September because our parks close for the winter. I just don't=
 see a clear way to make this puzzle work - but staying is one way, and per=
haps going to Kentucky in the spring. After April, when I finish at Honeyma=
n that season. I hope you see I'm trying here. I will stay if breaking my c=
ommitment would cause disharmony.

________________________________
From: Robert Samuel White
Sent: Thursday, February 6, 2025 7:15:49 PM
To: ALLEGRA Franki * OPRD <franki.allegra@oprd.oregon.gov<mailto:franki.all=
egra@oprd.oregon.gov>>
Subject: September

Hi, Franki.

I have a predicament.

On one hand, I want to establish a reliable relationship with you. I want y=
ou to know I'm dependable and you can count on me. This is really important=
 to me.

On the other hand, I really need to go home to Kentucky at some point. It i=
s very likely the last time I will ever see my mother. This is really impor=
tant to me too.

I was going to go this summer, but I couldn't turn down the Humbug position=
. Not only is it my favorite place on earth (literally), I get to experienc=
e it with the bustling summer activity of the coast!

And I was looking forward to the same kind of experience at Tugman in Septe=
mber, when the park is likely quite busy and active and I'd be responsible =
for greeting new visitors as relief host.

I really can't tell you how much it meant to me you extended the offer to m=
e and I want more than anything to do it. But I have a problem...

I started making plans to go home this winter and remembered why I came to =
Oregon in the first place: winters are harsh in Kentucky and the parks are =
closed. I literally can't travel there then.

After Umpqua in April, I spend two months at Humbug. I'd like to go home af=
ter that. But this means backing out of my September assignment at Tugman.

I know that you would accept this. But I need more than that from you. I ne=
ed to know you understand how torn I feel about it and that it's not a refl=
ection of my future reliability or passion for working with you at your par=
ks. And I need to know this won't hurt me - as you know I already backed ou=
t of the very dumb decision to go to a day use area away from the coast, an=
d I have no idea how that information appears in your systems.

I'm trying to build a new life here, but my old life has some loose ends I =
need to confront. Can you help me?

Sam


